en:
That's exactly why she clung to that painting even after she died, don't you think?
That's what I think.
Yeah, it's gotta be that.{p}

I bet they were up in her room, staring at her self-portraits the whole time.
The two of them, sitting shoulder to shoulder.
They were really close, like they were one body and one soul.{p}

That's what I thought.
Of course you're interested.
I mean, your life's riding on it.{p}

And I really did tail him well.
I never lost sight of him even once.
But then he suddenly vanished on me.{p}

There was no way he could've just disappeared.
There was absolutely no way he went into one of the houses nearby.
Past the corner he turned, there were high walls running on and on down both sides.{p}

...All right.
All of you are coming too, of course, right?
Then let's go.{p}

...Here we are, the art room door.
Ready?
I'm opening it.{p}

Did you see that, {a}?
You saw it just now, right? You definitely saw it.
The man painted in this picture crumbling away.{p}

Making accusations out of nowhere and then storming off angry. {f:What a horrible guy.|What a horrible person.}
{f:I|I} was appalled.
...But with Shindo gone, the mood somehow went flat.{p}

Heh, aren't you the tough one.
If you say you're fine, I won't force it on you.
But if you regret it later, it'll be too late, you hear?{p}

It must have been someone who'd seen that horrible face earlier{f:.|.}
Shindo glanced at {f:me|me}.
"You don't want to hear it, right? So I can go home now, huh?"
Without waiting for an answer, he was already on his feet.
"Wait a minute, Shindo!"
"No way. Well, take good care of your life while you can, all right?"{p}

Saying it mockingly, Shindo opened the door and walked out.
"Shindo!"
{f:I|I} hurried after him.{p}

I shoved his defenseless back.
Shindo pitched forward.
And then...{p}

......There was a sickening clunk.
Shindo slid limply to the floor.
The fire extinguisher, hidden behind Shindo until now, came into view.{p}

In my hazy vision, as I stared at his motionless back, a crowd of people came running in.
They must have heard the commotion{f:.|.}
But none of it mattered anymore.
Someone was talking to {f:me|me}, but I couldn't follow what they said.
{f:I|I} could only think about one thing: would Shimizu's curse reach me even inside the prison I was sure to be sent to...{p}

Whoa, whoa, knock it off.
Do I look like some creep who'd get obsessed with someone's photo album?
I'm talking about the paintings she kept in her room.{p}

Oh yeah, right around the time she started working on that painting, the two of us stopped seeing each other.
She stopped inviting me over.
Why do you think that was?{p}

She painted her dead pets, over and over.
She claimed that if you painted with all your heart and soul, a soul would come to dwell in the painting.
Whether that's true or not, maybe she thought painting her pets was bringing them back to life.{p}

Some time after that, on a day off, I think it was.
I heard this tremendous yelling coming from Shimizu's house.
I looked out the window to see what was going on, and there was that guy, running out of Shimizu's house!{p}

While I was wondering who should go next, the club room door opened.
"Hey, you lot, what are you doing? It's already time to go home."
It was a teacher making the rounds{f:.|.}{p}

{f:We|We} were chased out of the club room.
It was a shame after all the planning, but with an interruption like that, there was nothing to be done{f:.|.}
We decided to pick it up next time, and {f:we|we} split up.{p}

But even after everyone had gone home, {f:I|I} stayed behind.
I couldn't stop thinking about what Shindo had said, that something about the painting was bugging him{f:.|.}
Could Shindo have noticed something that {f:I|I} had missed{f:?|?}{p}

When I opened the art room door, the painting was still in the same place.
I crept closer to it.
The moment I peered into the painting, searching for anything strange...{p}

The eyes in the painting flashed.
At the same moment, my arms and legs went rigid.
{f:Was I paralyzed|I was paralyzed}★{p}

"I knew you'd come, {a}."
Shindo's voice came from behind me.
"You seemed like the curious type, so I figured if I said that, you'd come for sure."{p}
